## Addon

The addon talks to the game only through the public Blizzard UI API. No Blizzard code,
art, or data files are copied. The addon is MIT licensed.

## Bridge and plugin dependencies

The bridge and plugin are MIT licensed. They depend on third-party packages that keep
their own licenses; all are permissively licensed. The versions are pinned in
`bridge/uv.lock` and `bridge/pyproject.toml`.

| Component | License | Project |
|---|---|---|
| uv (downloaded by the bootstrap installer) | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/astral-sh/uv |
| CPython 3.12 (installed by uv) | PSF License Agreement | https://www.python.org/ |
| httpx | BSD-3-Clause | https://www.python-httpx.org/ |
| numpy | BSD-3-Clause | https://numpy.org/ |
| Pillow | HPND | https://python-pillow.org/ |
| mss (Windows only) | MIT | https://github.com/BoboTiG/python-mss |
| windows-capture (Windows only) | MIT | https://github.com/NiiightmareXD/windows-capture |
| PySide6 (optional `overlay` extra) | LGPL-3.0 (or GPL-3.0 / commercial) | https://www.qt.io/qt-for-python |

The bootstrap installer downloads uv from the official Astral GitHub release and
verifies its SHA256 before use. It never downloads or executes a script from a URL.

## Design input (read, not copied)

- `chelinho139/wow-ai` (MIT) — pixel-strip capture loop, slot installer bookkeeping
  (`ensure()`-style created/kept counting) and the silent-WAV doorbell idea.
- `Geraldlol/witchcraft` (MIT) — atomic slot writes with rename retries on Windows
  (WinError 5/32) and the click-through overlay toggle pattern.

No code was copied from unlicensed projects. Behaviour that follows published protocol
research lives in `docs/research/06-prior-art-and-transport-spec.md`.
